      "problem": "Simplify $(2x^2y^{-1})^{-4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of product rule and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}^{2}{y}^{-1})^{-4} & = \\\\ {2}^{-4}\\cdot ({x}^{2})^{-4}\\cdot ({y}^{-1})^{-4} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{4}}\\cdot {x}^{(2)(-4)}\\cdot {y}^{(-1)(-4)} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {x}^{-8}\\cdot {y}^{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{16}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{8}}\\cdot {y}^{4} & = \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{4}}{16{x}^{8}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
